  "$comment": "The committed registry of every estate-tax wizard tab (JRNY-06, plan 12-04). A step is DATA, never code. Every url carries ?tab= alone, read once at mount by readInitialTab() in EstateTaxWizard.tsx:55, so a tab is reachable without clicking the seven before it -- no record performs a click or a fill, because a click-through would not prove the URL seam JRNY-01 requires. Every record declares reset case-alpha-no-output. A tax tab mutates nothing itself, so noop would seem right -- but $caseId.tax.tsx:56 renders the header from `row.decedent_name ?? 'Decedent'`, and decedent_name is a column the SUCCESSION wizard's autosave writes. With noop these eight steps rendered 'Estate of Pedro' or 'Estate of Decedent' depending purely on whether a wizard step had run first, and all eight failed with diffPixels=947 the moment the full suite ran in registry order. A step must not depend on what ran before it; the reset makes the observed row deterministic. It is a restore, not a mutation. NO tax_input_json IS SEEDED anywhere in Phase 12; these tabs render the wizard's own createDefaultEstateTaxState() defaults, which is the state a lawyer opening the tax wizard for the first time actually sees. Each rubric PAIRS the selected tab button with the panel it renders: tab-<n>'s aria-selected must read true AND that tab's panel root must be the one visible AND the next tab's panel root must be absent, so a tab strip that highlights one tab while rendering another is red rather than green.",
